Now I have enough evidence to classify. Note the igmp.c case: `ih3 = igmpv3_query_hdr(skb)` at 1014 is a REFETCH after the pull — my scanner flagged uses at 1014 etc., but those are assignments refetching. So igmp is SAFE. Similarly ovs refetches vh at 461. exthdrs.c ipv6_dest_hao refetches hao and ipv6h after pskb_expand_head — SAFE. reassembly.c refetches hdr at 347 after pull — SAFE. wpa.c all three refetch ("reload hdr - skb might have been reallocated") — SAFE.

Remaining strong candidates for i013 (tx-cow-head-realloc on s04):

